1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,710
Bugs.

2
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:01,864
Feature requests.

3
00:00:01,864 --> 00:00:02,943
Escalations.

4
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:03,928
Alerts.

5
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,038
They arrive faster than anyone can work them.

6
00:00:06,038 --> 00:00:08,525
What is left over is the backlog.

7
00:00:08,725 --> 00:00:13,294
A software factory puts a coordinated fleet of specialist agents on that queue.

8
00:00:13,294 --> 00:00:19,277
Intake, triage, design, build, review — one request carried through to a change a person can read.

9
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:21,864
Underneath all of it sits a single claim.

10
00:00:21,864 --> 00:00:27,219
A modest model inside an excellent harness beats a frontier model inside a poor one.

11
00:00:27,219 --> 00:00:28,611
That is a hypothesis.

12
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,939
The experiment written to falsify it is pre-registered.

13
00:00:32,139 --> 00:00:35,258
Every subsystem exists because that claim depends on it.

14
00:00:35,258 --> 00:00:37,670
A context pack, budgeted and cited.

15
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:40,570
Typed tools, so anything computable is computed.

16
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,535
Confidence scored against outcomes.

17
00:00:42,535 --> 00:00:45,182
A blast radius the machine checks.

18
00:00:45,382 --> 00:00:46,272
Gates block.

19
00:00:46,272 --> 00:00:52,063
The keystone is regression proven: fix a defect and you owe a test that failed at the parent commit, for the right reason.

20
00:00:52,063 --> 00:00:55,631
A test that fails on a missing import proves the code did not exist.

21
00:00:55,631 --> 00:00:57,128
It is refused.

22
00:00:57,328 --> 00:01:00,682
A metric with no data reports its absence, not zero.

23
00:01:00,682 --> 00:01:04,730
Ask what the central bet has been shown, and today the answer is insufficient data.

24
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:06,208
No trials recorded.

25
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:08,041
A test keeps it that way.

26
00:01:08,241 --> 00:01:13,513
Same definition files, same harness, same guarantees — on a laptop, or in the cloud.

27
00:01:13,513 --> 00:01:15,737
No control plane you don't own.

28
00:01:15,937 --> 00:01:17,258
Software factory.

29
00:01:17,258 --> 00:01:19,965
Open source, Apache two point zero.
